<title>POLAND: Bank Komunalny falls on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Bank Komunalny falls on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Bank Komunalny w Gdyni SA, Wednesday's biggest loser fell 7.3 percent to 29.2 zlotys in a 3.5-million zloty trade on profit-taking after having risen 37 percent since its debut on September 18, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;It was bound to fall after such a surge,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
